Implementation constraints: Edit src/static/style.css. Append a new CSS rule block for [data-theme="midnight"]. Do not modify any existing blocks. Use the exact variable names and values specified below.

Behavioral specification: Add a CSS block:
[data-theme="midnight"] {
  --font: inherit;
  --bg: oklch(0.18 0 0);
  --panel: oklch(0.22 0.003 90);
  --text: oklch(0.92 0.01 90);
  --border: oklch(0.92 0.01 90 / 0.08);
}

Additionally, define the following variables within this block to match the phosphor theme's structure but with midnight values:
--sidebar-bg: oklch(0.16 0 0);
--sidebar-text: oklch(0.85 0.01 90);
--sidebar-border: oklch(0.85 0.01 90 / 0.08);
--sidebar-hover: oklch(0.22 0 0);
--sidebar-active: oklch(0.26 0.003 90);
--sidebar-active-bar: oklch(0.75 0.12 75);
--accent-primary: oklch(0.75 0.12 75);
--accent-secondary: oklch(0.72 0.06 220);
--accent-error: oklch(0.55 0.12 25);
--bubble-user: oklch(0.78 0.06 220);

Ensure text-shadow is explicitly set to none for all elements within this theme block if not already handled by inheritance, but specifically add:
[data-theme="midnight"] * {
  text-shadow: none;
}

Acceptance condition: The file contains a [data-theme="midnight"] selector with the specified variable definitions. No other theme blocks are modified.
